<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Daewoo gets 40 pct of Kazakhtelekom for $1.37 bln.</title>
<headline>Daewoo gets 40 pct of Kazakhtelekom for $1.37 bln.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daewoo Corp has bought a 40 percent stake in Kazakhstan's telecoms monopoly Kazakhtelekom for a total of $1.37 billion, government and Daewoo officials told a news conference on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;On May 31 Kazakhstan's government and Daewoo Corporation signed a contract... The value of the deal is $1.37 bln,&quot; a government press release said. &quot;Daewoo has bought a 40 percent stake,&quot; said Kazakhtelekom Chairman Serik Burkitbayev.</p>
</text>
